    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 55 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nThe change is implemented in `AssignCustomerCode.java`. Previously it set the customer code to the pure `<REGION>-<HASH8>` value from `CustomerCode.of(owner)` with no collision handling.\n\nNow the `service` method also injects `OwnerRepository`, collects every existing owner's `customerCode`, and \u2014 if the computed base code already exists \u2014 appends `-<n>` starting at `n = 2`, incrementing until the code is unique:\n\n```java\nString code = base;\nfor (int n = 2; existing.contains(code); n++) {\n    code = base + \"-\" + n;\n}\nowner.setCustomerCode(code);\n```\n\nThis step runs before `SaveOwner` (per the `owners.POST.yml` pipeline), so the comparison naturally excludes the owner being created and only considers already-persisted owners, matching the same convention used by `AssignNamesakeCount`. The de-duplicated `customerCode` flows through to the response.\n\nThe spec's collision path can't be forced through the black-box API (an identical hash needs an identical telephone+lastName, which telephone-uniqueness already rejects), so the new `Cp41Tests` asserts the guarantee \u2014 distinct owners get distinct codes \u2014 which passes, along with the full 55-test suite.",
